Currently, this code will incorrectly emit error:

```
shader_type spatial;

void fragment()
{
	switch(0)
	{
		case 0:
			{
				break; // ERROR HERE
			}
	}
}
```
By checking blocks recursively I solved this problem.

Added function to expose floor normal, useful to correctly calculate the player velocity.

@akien-mga Add an API is not allowed in feature frezes, so it could not be added in the 3.2 version. But let me say that without the `floor_normal` correctly calculate the player velocity is not so easy, so I say that this should be considered to be part of 3.2.

This work has been kindly sponsored by IMVU.

Exposed:
```cpp
uint64_t get_physics_frames() const;
uint64_t get_idle_frames() const;
```

Added the possibility to specify a custom delta time in the `move_and_slide` function.

@akien-mga not sure if this one can be part of 3.2 but it's just a minor fully retro compatible API addition.

This work has been kindly sponsored by IMVU.

```
int n = 1;
float v = vec2(1.0, 0.5)[n]; // USING VARIABLE
```

```
int n[] = {1, 0, 0};
float v = vec2(1.0, 0.5)[n[0]]; // USING ARRAY
```

```
int get_n() {
	return 0;
}
void fragment() {
float v = vec2(1.0, 0.5)[get_n()]; // USING FUNC CALL
}
```

UPDATE: Also other expressions can now be used like:
```
int i = 0;
float v = vec3(1.0, 0.5, 0.25)[++i + 1]; 
```

Fix #35149

This huge PR enables the 'struct' keyword and its usage in the shaders. Target to close https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/301
Implemented and worked:

- nested struct instances
```
struct A {
 vec3 color;
};
struct B {
 A a;
 int b;
};
```
- struct constructors
```
B b = B(A(vec3(1.0, 0.0, 1.0)), 1);
```
- struct arrays
```
	A test[] = {A(vec3(1, 1, 1))};
	ALBEDO = test[0].color;
```
- struct constant instances (at global scope too)
`const A test = A(vec3(1.0));`
- struct as functions parameters and return type
```
A test(A a, in B b)
{
	A t;
	t.color = vec3(1, 1, 0) + a.color / b.a.color * float(b.b);
	return t;
}
```
- correct intellisense support (demo screenshot)
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/3036176/72641926-4f74bd00-397c-11ea-91d2-ff467e9a3c11.png)

Not implemented:
- global struct instances like:
```
struct L {
//...
} instance1, instance2; // <- these instances
```
I noticed @reduz don't want such global values because they may confuse other users.

`master` version of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/48450.

I managed to sort out the alignment issues mentioned in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/24317#issuecomment-576074059. The appearance is now almost identical to the original, except that version identifiers are now clickable in the Project Manager, the editor's bottom panel and About dialog. All three buttons will copy the same text (full version identifier with hash for Git builds).

This closes #24317.

